{
    "word": "heterotropic",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4c2d3842-959d-3d8e-80f9-8fb822b45496",
                "word": "heterotropic",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08ed47a8-3452-3d09-83fa-5432ffa76682",
                        "entry_id": "4c2d3842-959d-3d8e-80f9-8fb822b45496",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Concerning an effect in one entity that is controlled or influenced by a separate entity, such as when one ligand influences the binding of another ligand."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12a7a834-0827-42f2-b040-1bb53eb2dac8",
                                "sense_id": "08ed47a8-3452-3d09-83fa-5432ffa76682",
                                "text": "This behavior is analogous to that of any cooperative binding protein, such as hemoglobin (18, 19 ), although in this case, cooperativity is observed between heterotropic rather than homotropic ligands."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79375de7-476f-4810-91f6-c291a8ef44c8",
                                "sense_id": "08ed47a8-3452-3d09-83fa-5432ffa76682",
                                "text": "Some allosteric enzymes exhibit mixed homotropic and heterotropic interactions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70653823-8dde-420e-95ab-deb8179deb13",
                                "sense_id": "08ed47a8-3452-3d09-83fa-5432ffa76682",
                                "text": "In heterotropic allosteric regulation, the bacterial enzymes are activated by ADP and inhibited by phosphoenolpyruvate binding at the allosteric site."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "319d3fd1-d93b-3e4b-a51f-7540c244adb5",
                        "entry_id": "4c2d3842-959d-3d8e-80f9-8fb822b45496",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Concerning a process that abnormally takes place outside of its normal system as well as within its normal system."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bbc8b8b-2008-424b-a842-29edb61714a4",
                                "sense_id": "319d3fd1-d93b-3e4b-a51f-7540c244adb5",
                                "text": "Heterotropic pregnancy occurs when intrauterine and ectopic pregnancies coexist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91c9a911-3a71-4961-8290-1449c22cc8c3",
                                "sense_id": "319d3fd1-d93b-3e4b-a51f-7540c244adb5",
                                "text": "Various hereditary conditions and congenital condition give rise to heterotropic calcification something abnormal in metabolic and endocrinal functions also give rise to deposition of calcium in extraskeletal system."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "488548df-a5a7-3f37-a59f-e8d8544c3987",
                        "entry_id": "4c2d3842-959d-3d8e-80f9-8fb822b45496",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Arising from the interaction of separate people or entities."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "646bb450-f366-465b-a5bb-ea7e5c269478",
                                "sense_id": "488548df-a5a7-3f37-a59f-e8d8544c3987",
                                "text": "At the end of the twentieth century Nature is alive and well, permeating the experience of everyday life as a riotous profusion of heterotropic images, signs and discursive constructs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db9450a5-02be-4190-9982-ab8c7722f2a5",
                                "sense_id": "488548df-a5a7-3f37-a59f-e8d8544c3987",
                                "text": "In contrast, heterotropic intentional mental states, intentional acts and actions cannot be performed and experienced by a single individual: heterotropic states, acts and actions necessarily refer to and depend on other individuals, i.e. they involve at least two individuals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d4109b1-26f8-4efc-a7da-08c5179685d7",
                                "sense_id": "488548df-a5a7-3f37-a59f-e8d8544c3987",
                                "text": "As Webster informs us, it is both psychomorphic and heterotropic. I suppose that's a fancy way of saying Illyrion is many things to many men."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
